{# Shared FEP header. Deliberately NOT an include of common.in.j2: three of its
   settings must differ, and each difference is load-bearing.

     1. pair_style is the soft-core variant, so pair_coeff takes a third
        argument (lambda) that the plain style rejects.
     2. `tail yes` is refused by compute fep for soft styles (LAMMPS errors with
        "Pair style does not support compute fep tail"), so the long-range LJ
        correction is omitted here and added analytically in post-processing by
        aemwater.fep.ghost.tail_correction.
     3. kspace accuracy is tightened to fep.kspace_accuracy. The default 1e-4 is
        fine for forces but puts ~0.016 kcal/mol of grid error into each
        charge-leg dU, which does not average out.

   Inheriting from common.in.j2 and overriding would leave the plain pair_style
   in the file above the override, so a template edit could silently reinstate
   the wrong Hamiltonian. #}
# {{ title }}
# generated by aemwater -- do not edit; edit the template instead
# FEP {{ leg }} leg, lambda_lj = {{ "%.4f"|format(lambda_lj) }}, lambda_q = {{ "%.4f"|format(lambda_q) }}

units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p

# n alpha_LJ alpha_C cutoff_LJ cutoff_coul. At lambda = 1 this reduces to
# lj/cut/coul/long to within kspace noise (verified: 2.4e-7 relative on the
# runner binary, docs/fep_design.md), so the coupled endpoint is the same physics
# the rest of the workflow uses.
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long/soft {{ fep.soft_core_n }} {{ fep.alpha_lj }} {{ fep.alpha_coul }} {{ md.cutoff }} {{ md.cutoff }}
# Arithmetic mixing for GAFF2, as elsewhere. No `tail yes` -- see header note 2.
pair_modify     mix arithmetic
kspace_style    pppm {{ fep.kspace_accuracy }}
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     harmonic
dihedral_style  charmm
improper_style  cvff
special_bonds   lj 0.0 0.0 0.5 coul 0.0 0.0 0.8333333333

# Charges for this state are baked into the data file rather than scaled at
# runtime: PPPM builds its grid at setup, and a per-state data file makes each
# lambda directory independently re-runnable.
read_data       {{ data_file }}

# Every i <= j pair is written explicitly. LAMMPS refuses to MIX two types whose
# lambdas differ ("Pair lj/cut/soft different lambda values in mix"), so a
# missing cross term is a hard error rather than a silently wrong Hamiltonian --
# but relying on that is relying on an error message, so nothing is left to
# mixing here.
{% for line in ghost_pair_coeffs -%}
{{ line }}
{% endfor %}
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes
comm_modify     cutoff {{ comm_cutoff }}

group           polymer molecule <> 1 {{ groups.n_polymer_molecules }}
{% if groups.n_ion_molecules > 0 -%}
group           ions molecule <> {{ groups.n_polymer_molecules + 1 }} {{ groups.n_polymer_molecules + groups.n_ion_molecules }}
{% endif -%}
# Resident water only. The ghost is excluded so that thermostatting, density and
# any per-group average describe the physical system rather than the system plus
# a phantom.
group           water type {{ groups.water_type_o }} {{ groups.water_type_h }}
group           ghost type {{ ghost.type_o }} {{ ghost.type_h }}
group           real subtract all ghost

thermo          {{ md.thermo_every }}
thermo_style    custom step temp press vol density etotal ke pe ebond eangle edihed evdwl ecoul elong
thermo_modify   flush yes
